     "lesson": "When picking a pen lying flat on the table, lower the grasp height several millimeters below the object's top surface so the fingertips extend to the table surface and reliably enclose the thin body."
    },
    {
     "n": 2,
     "code": "# Look at the current scene: the pen is already inside magenta_holder, but leaning / not standing fully (height 0.1245, top_z 0.9245, horizontal_span ~ 0.08m).\n# It's at [0.0625, 0.1101, 0.8623], rim_height=0.08.\n# We need to grasp the pen standing/leaning in the holder, lift it up, reorient vertically or let it drop straight so it stands upright.\nobs = observe()\npen = obs[\"objects\"][\"purple_pen\"]\nholder = obs[\"zones\"][\"magenta_holder\"]\ntable_z = obs[\"table_z\"]\nh_x, h_y = holder[\"center\"][0], holder[\"center\"][1]\n\ncands = grasp_candidates(\"purple_pen\")\n# Grasp candidate near the top/middle of the pen sticking out of holder\ncands = [c for c in cands if c.get(\"fits_open_fingers\", True)]\n# Sort by height descending to grab the top sticking out of the holder\ncands.sort(key=lambda c: c[\"height\"], reverse=True)\n\nif cands:\n    best_cand = cands[0]\n    # adjust grasp height if needed to be well above rim (rim is 0.08m above table)\n    if best_cand[\"height\"] < 0.09:\n        best_cand[\"height\"] = 0.095\n    grasp(best_cand)\n\n# Lift up vertically above the holder\nmove_by(dz=0.15)\n\n# Align directly over holder center and orient vertically\nsafe_z = table_z + holder[\"rim_height\"] + 0.12\n# Orient pen upright using reorient helper or vertical grip\nreorient_held_object_upright(h_x, h_y, safe_z)\n\n# Lower into container until slightly above base/rim, then drop\ndrop_into_container_v2(\"purple_pen\", \"magenta_holder\", safe_z_offset=0.08)",
